  "description": "One of Haro's most popular full suspension bikes, the Shift R7 is made with 6061-T6 alloy and features an internal tapered head tube & Haro's Four-Bar linkage design. At the heart of the design is a Trail suspension platform that promotes pedaling with a central linkage and chainstay pivots that optimize shock performance. This design isolates the rear shock from braking forces while keeping the suspension active when needed. The R7 uses RockShox' s new Recon Gold RL Boost suspension fork with 130mm of travel. Its semi-complete Shimano SLX 1X11 drive train forms a unique partnership with an FSA V-Drive Modular Boost crankset equipped with a 32t alloy chain ring. The Shift R7 features U28 TL tubeless compatible double wall rims with Kenda Nevegal 27.5 x 2.35\" 60 tpi tires and includes a TranzX internal dropper post for on-the-fly seat height adjustments.\n6061-T6 alloy 4-Bar Linkage frame, 125mm rear travel, tapered head tube, 73mm BB shell, Boost thru-axle dropouts\nMonarch RL Solo Air rear shock w/ rebound adjuster & lockout\nNew Rockshox Recon Gold RL 27.5\" Boost fork, 130mm travel\nFSA V-Drive Modular Boost crankset w/ 32T alloy chainring\nShimano SLX 1x11-spd rear derailleur, Shadow Plus\nShimano SLX 1x11 shifter & 11-46T cassette\nRitchey Trail alloy cockpit w/ Trail WCS Lock-Ring grips\nNew Deore M500 disc brakes\nTranzX JD-YSP15 internal dropper post",
